---
// Unlisted pitch deck for Request for Founders, thesis 4. Not linked from the site, noindex.
const total = 13;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#15211A" />
    <title>Runs Without You · Bunyasit Fang</title>
    <meta name="description" content="The back office engine for Thai small businesses. Request for Founders, thesis 4." />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main id="deck">
      <!-- 1 Title -->
      <section class="slide dark title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Request for Founders · Thesis 4</p>
        <h1>Runs Without You</h1>
        <p class="sub">The back office engine for Thai small businesses</p>
        <p class="meta">Bunyasit Fang · October 2026</p>
      </section>

      <!-- 2 Owner -->
      <section class="slide">
        <h2>I am the owner, many times over</h2>
        <div class="cards three">
          <div class="card stat"><b>51%</b><p>of Onecha, a matcha import and resale business I run today</p></div>
          <div class="card stat"><b>1</b><p>cafe founded and operated: JOJO Soba, coffee and soba in Bangkok</p></div>
          <div class="card stat"><b class="ph">[N]</b><p>businesses in my family's portfolio, where I sit inside operations</p></div>
        </div>
        <p class="lead">I do not study the admin problem. I live it, across several businesses, and I build AI systems for a living.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- 3 Four jobs -->
      <section class="slide">
        <h2>Four jobs that only the owner can do today</h2>
        <div class="cards two">
          <div class="card"><h3>Buying and selling</h3><p>Orders arrive in LINE and Shopee. Purchase orders, invoices, slips and stock are reconciled by hand every night.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Finding and talking to suppliers</h3><p>Sourcing matcha grades from Japan means hours of searching, emailing and negotiating in two languages.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Import and legal paperwork</h3><p>Customs declarations, FDA registration and tax invoices are checked by one person who knows where everything is.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Hiring freelancers</h3><p>Designers, content and delivery help are found, briefed, chased and paid one chat thread at a time.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 4 Dashboard vs engine -->
      <section class="slide">
        <h2>Owners do not need another dashboard. They need hands</h2>
        <div class="cards two">
          <div class="card muted">
            <h3>Today: a dashboard</h3>
            <ul><li>Owner types in data</li><li>Software shows it back as a chart</li><li>Owner still does the task</li><li>Adoption dies after week two</li></ul>
          </div>
          <div class="card accent">
            <h3>Ours: an engine</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Reads what already exists: LINE, slips, bank SMS, email, customs portals</li>
              <li>Completes the task: books the entry, drafts the PO, checks the document, briefs the freelancer</li>
              <li>Owner approves with one tap</li>
              <li>Admin drops from hours to minutes a day</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 5 Onecha pilot -->
      <section class="slide">
        <h2>Onecha is the pilot: one matcha order, end to end</h2>
        <div class="cards five">
          <div class="card"><h3>Source</h3><p>Agent shortlists Japanese suppliers by grade and price, drafts the first email in Japanese</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Buy</h3><p>Negotiation thread summarised, PO drafted, payment scheduled on approval</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Import</h3><p>Customs and FDA documents cross-checked against the PO before anything ships</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Sell</h3><p>LINE and Shopee orders turned into invoices and stock movements automatically</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Staff</h3><p>Freelancers for content and delivery briefed, tracked and paid from one queue</p></div>
        </div>
        <p class="lead">I control Onecha, so the engine goes live on day one with no sales cycle, and the hours saved are measured honestly.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- 6 Loops -->
      <section class="slide">
        <h2>Three loops, and nothing executes without a tap</h2>
        <div class="cards three">
          <div class="card"><h3>1 · Ingest</h3><p>Connects LINE, email, bank notifications, Shopee and the POS. Reads Thai, Japanese and English receipts, slips and chats.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>2 · Decide</h3><p>An agent proposes the next action with the source evidence attached: the slip, the message, the clause it checked.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>3 · Approve</h3><p>Owner taps yes in LINE. Autonomy widens per task as the approval rate stays high. Trust is earned, not assumed.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 7 Why now -->
      <section class="slide">
        <h2>Why this works in 2026 and did not in 2022</h2>
        <div class="cards three">
          <div class="card"><h3>Models read messy records</h3><p>LLMs now handle Thai receipts, Japanese supplier emails and customs forms reliably. The tasks were never hard, the reading was.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>The records are already digital</h3><p>PromptPay, e-tax invoices and marketplace exports mean the evidence exists. Nobody has to type it in.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Owners live in LINE</h3><p>No new app to adopt. The engine speaks where the business already runs, in the owner's chat.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 8 Why me -->
      <section class="slide">
        <h2>Why me: operator, AI builder, shipper</h2>
        <div class="cards three">
          <div class="card"><h3>Operator</h3><p>Majority owner of Onecha. Founded and ran JOJO Soba. Sit inside the operations of my family's portfolio of Thai SMBs.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>AI veteran</h3><p>PassionSeed to 300 users in a month. CareerAc, Hive (Gemini hackathon semi-finalist), NeuralMix. Built RocketMap, an AI hypothesis-testing canvas, and used it to de-risk this idea.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Shipper</h3><p>LongKeeb shipped mechanical keyboards to paying customers worldwide. I have run procurement, manufacturing and fulfilment myself.</p></div>
        </div>
        <p class="lead small">Chulalongkorn BAScii, Integrated Innovation · Berkeley SCET Startup Semester · 30+ shipped projects</p>
      </section>

      <!-- 9 Investor's seat -->
      <section class="slide">
        <h2>What I see from the investor's seat</h2>
        <p class="lead">Across the family portfolio, the businesses that survive share habits the ones that fail do not. The engine encodes the survivors' habits so every owner gets them by default.</p>
        <div class="cards two">
          <div class="card accent">
            <h3>Survivors</h3>
            <ul>
              <li class="ph">[Habit 1: e.g. reorder before stock-out, not after]</li>
              <li class="ph">[Habit 2: e.g. every slip reconciled the same day]</li>
              <li class="ph">[Habit 3: e.g. documents checked before the shipment leaves]</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="card muted">
            <h3>Failures</h3>
            <ul>
              <li class="ph">[Anti-habit 1]</li>
              <li class="ph">[Anti-habit 2]</li>
              <li class="ph">[Anti-habit 3]</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 10 De-risked -->
      <section class="slide">
        <h2>De-risked before applying, with theory and AI</h2>
        <p class="lead">I built RocketMap, an AI business model canvas that turns a venture into ranked hypotheses and tests them against theory and evidence. I ran this idea through it first. The riskiest assumptions, and where each stands:</p>
        <div class="cards three">
          <div class="card"><h3>Desirability</h3><p>Owners will hand admin to an agent if every action shows its evidence</p><p class="result ph">Tested at Onecha: [result]</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Feasibility</h3><p>LLMs read Thai slips, Japanese supplier mail and customs forms accurately enough</p><p class="result ph">Prototype on Onecha records: [accuracy]</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Viability</h3><p>Owners pay more than a bookkeeper hour a week for hours saved every day</p><p class="result ph">[N] portfolio owners asked: [result]</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 11 Business model -->
      <section class="slide">
        <h2>Business model and market</h2>
        <div class="cards three">
          <div class="card stat"><b class="ph">฿[X] / mo</b><p>per business, priced below one bookkeeper hour a week</p></div>
          <div class="card stat"><b>Take rate</b><p>on payments and supplier orders routed through the engine, later</p></div>
          <div class="card stat"><b>~3M</b><p>registered Thai SMEs, most with fewer than ten staff</p></div>
        </div>
        <p class="lead"><strong>Wedge.</strong> Import-and-resell traders and small F&amp;B in Bangkok, starting with Onecha and the family portfolio. Expansion follows LINE and QR payment behaviour across Southeast Asia: Vietnam, Indonesia, the Philippines.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- 12 Plan -->
      <section class="slide">
        <h2>Twelve weeks to a live engine and paying owners</h2>
        <div class="cards three">
          <div class="card"><span class="tag">Weeks 1 to 4</span><h3>Onecha live</h3><p>Ingest LINE, email and slips. Supplier sourcing and PO drafting loop running on real Onecha orders.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><span class="tag">Weeks 5 to 8</span><h3>Portfolio pilots</h3><p>Five businesses from the family portfolio onboarded. Import document check and freelancer queue added.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><span class="tag">Weeks 9 to 12</span><h3>Prove and convert</h3><p>Measure hours saved and errors caught. Convert pilots to paid. Pitch on December 4 with live customers.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 13 Ask -->
      <section class="slide dark title">
        <p class="eyebrow">The ask</p>
        <h1>1,000,000 THB</h1>
        <p class="sub">Twelve months of runway, one engineer, and LINE, bank and customs integration costs.</p>
        <p class="sub">Milestone: fifty paying businesses, each owner spending under five minutes a day on admin.</p>
        <p class="meta">bunyasit@passionseed.org · bigf.me · github.com/xb1g</p>
      </section>
    </main>

    <nav id="hud" aria-label="Slide navigation">
      <button id="prev" aria-label="Previous slide">←</button>
      <span id="count">1 / {total}</span>
      <button id="next" aria-label="Next slide">→</button>
    </nav>

    <script is:inline define:vars={{ total }}>
      const deck = document.getElementById('deck');
      const slides = [...deck.querySelectorAll('.slide')];
      const count = document.getElementById('count');
      const current = () => Math.round(deck.scrollLeft / deck.clientWidth);
      const go = (i) => {
        const n = Math.max(0, Math.min(total - 1, i));
        deck.scrollTo({ left: n * deck.clientWidth, behavior: 'smooth' });
      };
      deck.addEventListener('scroll', () => {
        const n = current();
        count.textContent = `${n + 1} / ${total}`;
        history.replaceState(null, '', `#${n + 1}`);
      }, { passive: true });
      document.getElementById('prev').onclick = () => go(current() - 1);
      document.getElementById('next').onclick = () => go(current() + 1);
      addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
        if (['ArrowRight', 'PageDown', ' '].includes(e.key)) { e.preventDefault(); go(current() + 1); }
        if (['ArrowLeft', 'PageUp'].includes(e.key)) { e.preventDefault(); go(current() - 1); }
        if (e.key === 'Home') go(0);
        if (e.key === 'End') go(total - 1);
      });
      const start = parseInt(location.hash.slice(1), 10);
      if (start > 1 && start <= slides.length) deck.scrollTo({ left: (start - 1) * deck.clientWidth });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>

<style is:global>
  :root {
    --dk: #15211a; --dk2: #3b5c3c; --lt: #eef3ea; --green: #6e9b3e; --gold: #c9a227; --deep: #2e6b4f;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; }
  html, body { height: 100%; background: var(--dk); font-family: Calibri, 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif; color: var(--dk); }
  #deck { display: flex; height: 100dvh; overflow-x: auto; overflow-y: hidden; scroll-snap-type: x mandatory; scrollbar-width: none; }
  #deck::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }
  .slide {
    flex: 0 0 100vw; height: 100dvh; scroll-snap-align: start; overflow-y: auto;
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 4.5rem) clamp(1.25rem, 6vw, 5.5rem) 5rem;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; gap: clamp(1rem, 2.5vw, 2rem);
    background: var(--lt);
  }
  .slide.dark { background: var(--dk); color: #fff; }
  h1, h2, h3, b { font-family: Cambria, Georgia, serif; }
  h2 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 3rem); line-height: 1.15; color: var(--dk); border-left: 6px solid var(--gold); padding-left: 1rem; }
  h3 { font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2vw, 1.5rem); color: var(--deep); margin-bottom: .5rem; }
  p, li { font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.7vw, 1.3rem); line-height: 1.45; color: #2c3a30; }
  .lead { font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.9vw, 1.5rem); color: var(--dk2); max-width: 60rem; }
  .lead.small { font-size: clamp(.95rem, 1.5vw, 1.15rem); }
  .cards { display: grid; gap: clamp(.75rem, 1.5vw, 1.25rem); }
  .cards.two { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
  .cards.three { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  .cards.five { grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr); }
  .card { background: #fff; border-radius: 12px; border-top: 5px solid var(--green); padding: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.6rem); box-shadow: 0 2px 10px rgba(21, 33, 26, .08); }
  .card.accent { background: var(--deep); border-top-color: var(--gold); }
  .card.accent h3, .card.accent li, .card.accent p { color: #fff; }
  .card.muted { background: #dfe7da; border-top-color: #9aa89a; }
  .card ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; display: grid; gap: .5rem; }
  .card.stat { text-align: center; }
  .card.stat b { display: block; font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.6rem); color: var(--green); line-height: 1.1; margin-bottom: .5rem; }
  .card .result { margin-top: .9rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--dk); }
  .tag { display: inline-block; font-size: .85rem; font-weight: 700; background: var(--gold); color: var(--dk); padding: .15rem .6rem; border-radius: 999px; margin-bottom: .6rem; }
  .ph { background: rgba(201, 162, 39, .25); border-radius: 4px; }
  .card.accent .ph { background: rgba(201, 162, 39, .35); }
  .title { justify-content: center; }
  .title h1 { font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 8vw, 6rem); color: var(--green); line-height: 1.05; }
  .title .sub { font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2.4vw, 1.8rem); color: #dfe9d8; max-width: 52rem; }
  .eyebrow { color: var(--gold) !important; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .15em; font-size: clamp(.8rem, 1.4vw, 1rem) !important; font-weight: 700; }
  .meta { color: #9fb39a !important; font-size: clamp(.9rem, 1.4vw, 1.1rem) !important; }
  #hud { position: fixed; bottom: 1rem; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .75rem; background: rgba(21, 33, 26, .85); color: #fff; padding: .35rem .6rem; border-radius: 999px; z-index: 10; backdrop-filter: blur(6px); }
  #hud button { background: none; border: 0; color: #fff; font-size: 1.25rem; cursor: pointer; padding: .25rem .6rem; border-radius: 999px; }
  #hud button:hover { background: var(--deep); }
  #count { font-size: .95rem; min-width: 4rem; text-align: center; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .cards.two, .cards.three, .cards.five { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .slide { justify-content: flex-start; }
  }
  @media (min-width: 821px) and (max-width: 1100px) { .cards.five { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
</style>
